{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes","id":1097996,"title":"In-Universe Reasons for why so many Things have Banes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T23:35:55-07:00","id":1097996,"title":"In-Universe Reasons for why so many Things have Banes?","content":"Werewolves are allergic to silver, vampires can be killed with sun and fire, fire also works for Prometheans, spirits suffer from bans, destinies have corresponding dooms, Changelings are allergic to cold iron, True Fae are prohibited from giving their opponents impossible tasks, changeling contracts have catches, slashers have frailties, Proximus dynasties have curses, the Underworld's rivers are both mystically potent and largely poisonous, and there's probably more examples that I'm not remembering.<br /> <br /> It seems to be a rule that things with magical power always have weaknesses, from an out-of-universe perspective this is mostly to allow clever characters to defeat opponents they can't overpower, to prevent players from ignoring the threat posed by hunters, and to force certain NPCs (spirits, slashers etc.) to behave in-character.<br /> <br /> For an occultist living in the Chronicles, how do they explain this phenomena? For Changelings, it seems straightforward to say that the Wyrd thinks it's boring for the strong to always win and arranges scenarios where they can be defeated. Mages probably blame the Abyss somehow But what about say Promethean mystics or Ordo Dracul scholars? What theories could a character who notices this trend come up with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:42:02-07:00","id":1097998,"title":"","content":"easy the would really is shattered in a vary real way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13426-ameraaaaaa","name":"Ameraaaaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:48:58-07:00","id":1098001,"title":"","content":"I'd blame the Dark Mother wanting there to be innate flaws in all her children so heroes can defeat them (and increase the chances of it only being heroes who defeat the monsters rather than random people).<br /> <br /> I thought about this abit when I was trying to think up if my fansplat should have a bane... Justifying banes can sometimes be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-29-2017, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:59:56-07:00","id":1098007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes?p=1097998#post1097998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">easy the would really is shattered in a vary real way</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that in the same sense as the world being &quot;fallen&quot; or do you mean something different?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes?p=1098001#post1098001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd blame the Dark Mother wanting there to be innate flaws in all her children so heroes can defeat them (and increase the chances of it only being heroes who defeat the monsters rather than random people).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see two problems with that. 1) It doesn't explain the banes of Abyssal spirits and angels, which to my knowledge aren't related to the Dark Mother 2) I'm not sure how it increases the chance of heroes rather than random people defeating them. Aren't heroes much more capable of taking monsters in straight fights than the average hunter / blue-book character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","user":"jsnider3","date":"to 05-29-2017, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:07:09-07:00","id":1098008,"title":"","content":"Mine is simple - <b>'World is Broken'</b> - In Chronicles of Darkness universe there is something inherently <i>wrong</i> with the reality. Most of the time everything sounds about 'realistic', like things running in real world, but on some instinctual level, you know, all of us know living in this world, that there is somewhere one big crack in universe and it's resonate through the cosmos, in subtle ways. Maybe it's primal origin of monster races? Maybe it's just cruel joke of ( The First and Greatest ) Demiurge? Was it Abyss, Fall of Pangea, creation of Gentry, first instance when Flux broke from Pyros - it's irrelevant. Once set in cosmos, it's repeats itself everywhere, like dark ripple on the surface of water.<br /> <br /> World in Chronicles of Darkness is <b><i>dark</i></b> - It's called Modern Gothic not without reason.<br /> <br /> And Banes are all those after effects marking monsters with this primordial flaw in universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:38:48-07:00","id":1098012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jsnider3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes?p=1098007#post1098007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see two problems with that. 1) It doesn't explain the banes of Abyssal spirits and angels, which two my knowledge aren't related to the Dark Mother 2) I'm not sure how it increases the chance of heroes rather than random people defeating them. Aren't heroes much more capable of taking monsters in straight fights than the average hunter / blue-book character?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Abyssals are kin according to the rules (though not according to Dave, but he is running off a different definition of Kin to the one in the book). As for angels, yeah, they'd be totally unrelated. But still, my explanation covers 99% of monsters. Probably hard to come up with a single In-Universe reason which covers 100% other than the above stated &quot;Breaking is a repeating pattern in the world's supernatural&quot;<br /> 2) Having a bane means the average person probably doesn't have ready access to whatever the creature's weakness it is if they get jumped by the monster. Heroes need to findout the bane of the monster and use that, rather than &quot;random american #13 shooting it in the face with his average shotgun&quot; defeating the monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-29-2017, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:45:37-07:00","id":1098013,"title":"","content":"Oh, if we're considering &quot;The Dark Mother did it.&quot;, we should also consider &quot;The Exarchs did it. Most likely Ruin and Nemesis.&quot;, which is technically distinct from &quot;The Abyss did it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13248-jsnider3","name":"jsnider3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T02:47:15-07:00","id":1098042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes?p=1098012#post1098012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Abyssals are kin according to the rules</div> </div> </div> </div>Honest question: Where in the rules is that written?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:04:43-07:00","id":1098043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1097996-in-universe-reasons-for-why-so-many-things-have-banes?p=1098042#post1098042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honest question: Where in the rules is that written?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kin rules, it says supernatural entities which were never human are considered kin. (Later in the book there is even a nightmare which interacts with the abyss).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:36:42-07:00","id":1098049,"title":"","content":"It says that such creatures in general are considered kin. Even without Dave's input I'd probably have abyssal entities be one of the exceptions, just like GM-demons.<br /> I can also point out that Kinship Nightmares are based on fears represented by the Kin in some way. It is the fear of the Abyss that is the basis for The Void is Waiting. You might notice that the Nightmare affects all supernatural powers instead of only Supernal, and that feeding the Abyss with such power has zero risk of abyssal manifestations (unlike how it is when you literally feed the Abyss).<br /> But thanks for the answer. And, of course, the book doesn't actually state that abyssals are an exception so abyssal kinship doesn't go against RAW.<br /> <br /> Edit: Of course, due to the nature of abyssal entities it would also make perfect sense to have only some of them be Kin while others aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-29-2017, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:52:35-07:00","id":1098080,"title":"","content":"Expending idea of 'World is Broken' and marrying it with Dark Mother - I would say that she is Astral manifestation of this 'brokeness' of reality - and every monster with it's Bane resonate with her, on some level by this link. God Machine, then, separated from Dark Mother is outside of being Kin AND still his creation having Banes - it's because G-M is <i>other</i> source of 'brokeness', literal Demiurge ( or what's left of him ) in reality, probably that started this whole phenomena. And Ain Soph is just somewhere there, watching or not reality as it is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:57:22-07:00","id":1098081,"title":"","content":"A credible related theory- most supernatural creatures are immune/resistant to disease. A sign of supernatural power... or a sign that disease is <i>humanity's </i>bane?<br /> <br /> To answer the question, some theories:<ul><li>The godmachine/exarchs/both did it, ensuring supernaturals have reason not to just rule the world in broad daylight.</li> <li>Vampires were, seemingly, created by a curse- so were all the rest, and the banes remind them that they are not meant to be gods.</li> <li>It all comes from arcadia and runs on story logic, and what good is a story with an invincible character?,</li> <li>The underworld infests everything, ensuring all supernaturals have some rot in their nature. Now everything, even immortals, can die.</li> <li>The existence of prometheans and pandorans is a metaphysical abomination, and has spread flux everywhere, corrupting and breaking the supernatural.</li> <li>The abyss doesn't just stop the supernal- it tries to stop all magic, and these are its ways of dealing with the rest.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T07:47:02-07:00","id":1098102,"title":"","content":"Why do humans fall unconcious when they get hit in the head? Why do fleshy beings suffer from snake venom in their blood? Its just the way their eldritch biiology works. Like developing an allergy. Sunlight hurts vampires because it causes an oxydation-like effect on the vampire &quot;curse.&quot; Werewolves react badly to silver possibly because it creates an imbalance of lunar energy in their bodies. And so on. <br /> <br /> Banes are just a special name people use for specific magical alergies that are developed for a wide variety of reasons. Some supernaturals have multiple banes instead of just one. Some have no banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T18:41:15-07:00","id":1098309,"title":"","content":"I tend to view it as the world possessing metaphysical laws as well as physical ones. These laws operate on physics of symbolism and in this occult but essentially ordered system things have banes because that's just how they interact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}